---
// DESIGNED docs page for tools/autoskin (docs-thread relay R1, 2026-07-17; copy source:
// MrMiata workspace/2026-07-17_component-docs/for-humans/autoskin.md). Shared furniture:
// designed-doc.css. AutoSkin supersedes the retired ml-auto-skin ("BindSkin Tools") page.
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import '../../../styles/designed-doc.css';

const SUMMARY =
  'One button that skins your character for you. Pick the joints and the mesh, press Bind Skin, and AutoSkin works out the weights.';

const TITLE = 'AUTO SKIN';
const TRI = ['t-bone', 't-plasma', 't-ember'];
// The cycle counts glyphs only, continuing across word gaps (Claude Design's treatment).
let li = 0;
const titleGlyphs = TITLE.split('').map((ch) => ({ ch, cls: ch === ' ' ? 't-gap' : TRI[li++ % 3] }));
---
<DocsLayout title="Auto Skin | FabricatorStudio Docs" description={SUMMARY}>
  <article class="dd">
    <a class="dd-breadcrumb" href="/docs/">Docs</a>

    <header class="dd-header">
      <div class="dd-eyebrow">FABRICATOR &middot; SKINNING TOOL</div>
      <h1 class="dd-title" aria-label={TITLE}>
        {titleGlyphs.map((g) =>
          g.cls === 't-gap' ? <span class="t-gap"></span> : <span aria-hidden="true" class={g.cls}>{g.ch}</span>
        )}
      </h1>
      <p class="dd-summary">{SUMMARY}</p>
    </header>

    <!-- WHAT IT DOES -->
    <section class="dd-panel" aria-labelledby="as-what">
      <div class="dd-panel__head">
        <h2 id="as-what" class="dd-label dd-label--plasma">WHAT IT DOES</h2>
        <p class="dd-lede">One button and one checkbox</p>
      </div>
      <p class="dd-prose as-lede">AutoSkin skins your mesh for you. Pick your bind joints and your mesh, press <b class="b-plasma">Bind Skin</b>, and a smart engine works out the skin weights and puts them on. It can even build the skeleton for you if you do not have one yet. It is one button and one checkbox.</p>
      <div class="as-you-get">
        <p class="as-you-get__lede">You get:</p>
        <div class="dd-gets">
          <div class="dd-get"><span class="dd-get__glyph dd-get__glyph--circle" aria-hidden="true"></span><p>A <b>full skin in about two minutes</b>, with no weight painting to start from</p></div>
          <div class="dd-get"><span class="dd-get__glyph dd-get__glyph--diamond" aria-hidden="true"></span><p>An optional <b>Generate Joints</b> mode that builds a skeleton from the mesh alone</p></div>
          <div class="dd-get"><span class="dd-get__glyph dd-get__glyph--square" aria-hidden="true"></span><p>Any influences you painted by hand and locked left <b>exactly as they are</b></p></div>
          <div class="dd-get"><span class="dd-get__glyph dd-get__glyph--pill" aria-hidden="true"></span><p>One <b>Ctrl+Z</b> to undo the whole thing if you do not like it</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- GET STARTED -->
    <section class="dd-section" aria-labelledby="as-start">
      <div class="dd-panel__head dd-panel__head--bare">
        <h2 id="as-start" class="dd-label dd-label--plasma">GET STARTED</h2>
        <p class="dd-lede">Joints, mesh, Bind Skin</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="dd-steps">
        <li class="dd-step dd-step--plasma"><span class="dd-step__num">1</span><p>Install the engine the first time. AutoSkin tells you if anything is missing before it lets you run.</p></li>
        <li class="dd-step dd-step--plasma"><span class="dd-step__num">2</span><p>Select your bind joints and your mesh, the same as a normal smooth bind, and press <b class="b-plasma">Bind Skin</b>.</p></li>
        <li class="dd-step dd-step--plasma"><span class="dd-step__num">3</span><p>Watch it work: it exports, generates, matches to your skeleton, and applies. You can Cancel any time, and Maya never freezes.</p></li>
        <li class="dd-step dd-step--ember"><span class="dd-step__num">4</span><p>No skeleton yet? Tick <b class="b-ember">Generate Joints</b>, select just the mesh, and press Bind Skin. AutoSkin builds the joints and skins to them.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- GOOD TO KNOW -->
    <section class="dd-section" aria-labelledby="as-gtk">
      <div class="dd-panel__head dd-panel__head--bare">
        <h2 id="as-gtk" class="dd-label dd-label--ember">GOOD TO KNOW</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="dd-facts as-facts">
        <div class="dd-fact dd-fact--ember">
          <span class="dd-fact__num">1</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="dd-fact__name">Bind pose first</h3>
            <p class="dd-fact__line">Put your rig back at bind pose before re-skinning something that is already skinned. AutoSkin reads the rest shape, so skinning over a pose would bake that pose in.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="dd-fact dd-fact--ember">
          <span class="dd-fact__num">2</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="dd-fact__name">Fail loud, never bad</h3>
            <p class="dd-fact__line">Make sure the mesh actually sits on the skeleton and your joints all have different names. If not, AutoSkin stops and tells you instead of making a bad skin.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="dd-fact dd-fact--plasma">
          <span class="dd-fact__num">3</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="dd-fact__name">Locked means kept</h3>
            <p class="dd-fact__line">Locked influences are treated as "leave this alone" and kept exactly. Unlock any you want AutoSkin to weight for you.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="dd-fact dd-fact--plasma">
          <span class="dd-fact__num">4</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="dd-fact__name">Local, on your GPU</h3>
            <p class="dd-fact__line">It runs on your GPU, takes about two minutes per mesh, and never touches your original mesh while it works.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  /* Page-specific: layout only; everything else is shared furniture. */
  .as-lede { max-width: 58rem; }
  .as-you-get { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.75rem; }
  .as-you-get__lede { margin: 0; font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--bone-faint); }
  .as-facts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0.75rem; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .as-facts { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
